====Inflection====
* All the cases of ''kukaan'', except for the nominative singular, are old-fashioned. They can sometimes be used e.g. to arouse listeners' or readers' attention. In modern Finnish those cases have been replaced by the corresponding cases of ''[[kenkään]]'' &mdash; the nominative ''kenkään'' is, however, used only in poetic language, and even there very infrequently.
* Several of the singular cases of "ken" can be shortened by dropping -'''en''' from the stem, e.g. ''k'''''en'''''ellekään'' > ''kellekään''.
* Note like all Finnish personal pronouns, "kenkään" has the [[accusative]] form, '''''kenetkään'''''.
* There are also the abessive cases, but they are very infrequently used.
* There are also the instructive, temporal and causative cases, but they have by their meanings completely diverged from ''kukaan''.

